<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How TradeCommand collects, uses, stores and shares personal information, and how to contact us about it."
  updated="7 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    TradeCommand is job management software for trade businesses. It is made by TC Systems Pty Ltd
    (ABN 95 699 724 028) of 6 Lyster Street, Coffs Harbour NSW 2450, Australia. In this policy,
    "we", "us" and "our" mean TC Systems Pty Ltd, and "the service" means TradeCommand, including
    the app at app.tradecommand.com.au, the TradeCommand app for iPhone and iPad, and this
    website.
  </p>
  <p>
    We handle personal information under the Australian Privacy Act 1988 and the Australian Privacy
    Principles. This policy explains what we collect, why, where it goes, and how you can reach us.
  </p>

  <h2>Who the information is about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account holders and staff</strong> of a trade business that uses the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Clients and contacts</strong> of that business, whose details the business enters or receives.</li>
    <li><strong>People who message a business</strong> through a channel the business connects to the service, such as email or WhatsApp.</li>
    <li><strong>Visitors</strong> to this website.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, phone number and role in the business.</li>
    <li><strong>Business records:</strong> leads, quotes, jobs, variations, purchase orders, timesheets, invoices, comments and files that the business stores in the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Client details:</strong> names, addresses, phone numbers and email addresses that the business enters.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> the content, sender, recipient and timestamps of emails and WhatsApp messages sent to or from a connected channel.</li>
    <li><strong>Connected services:</strong> when a business connects Microsoft OneDrive, Microsoft Planner, Xero or WhatsApp, we store the access tokens and account identifiers those services give us.</li>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> when you clock in or out of a job, the app records your location at that moment, if you allow it. We do not track your location at any other time.</li>
    <li><strong>Photos:</strong> photos you take or choose to attach to a job.</li>
    <li><strong>Early access requests:</strong> the name, email address, phone number, business name, trade, team size and current software you enter in the early access form on this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser and device details, sign-in times, error reports, and a notification token for each device that allows push
      notifications.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect payment card numbers. We do not use cookies or trackers on this website for
    advertising. The app uses a session cookie so you stay signed in.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the service to the business and its staff.</li>
    <li>To reply to an early access request and send an invite code.</li>
    <li>To deliver and receive messages on a channel the business has connected.</li>
    <li>To let assistants in the service read incoming enquiries and turn them into leads, tasks or replies for a person to review.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure, fix faults and send service notices.</li>
    <li>To meet legal duties, such as tax and record-keeping rules.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Assistants and automated processing</h2>
  <p>
    The service includes assistants that read business records and messages to draft replies,
    classify enquiries and suggest actions. A person in the business reviews and takes each action.
    To run these assistants we send the relevant text to Anthropic, an AI model provider. Anthropic
    processes it to return a result and does not use it to train models.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only with providers that help us run the service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting and storage:</strong> our own servers and Amazon Web Services (S3) for files.</li>
    <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> MailPace, for transactional email.</li>
    <li><strong>Error monitoring:</strong> Sentry, for crash and error reports.</li>
    <li><strong>AI processing:</strong> Anthropic, as described above.</li>
    <li><strong>Push notifications:</strong> Apple, through the Apple Push Notification service, to deliver notifications to the iOS app.</li>
    <li><strong>Messaging platforms:</strong> Meta Platforms (WhatsApp Business Platform) and any messaging provider a business connects, for messages sent through that channel.</li>
    <li><strong>Connected services:</strong> Microsoft and Xero, only when a business connects them, and only for the data that connection needs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers store data outside Australia, including in the United States. We choose
    providers that commit to protecting personal information to a standard comparable to Australian law.
  </p>
  <p>We also disclose information when the law requires it, or to protect the rights, property or safety of people.</p>

  <h2>WhatsApp and Meta</h2>
  <p>
    A business can connect a WhatsApp Business account to the service. When it does, messages sent
    to that number are delivered to the service through Meta's WhatsApp Business Platform, and
    replies the business sends go back the same way. We use the information Meta gives us only to
    deliver those messages and to manage the connected account. Our use of information from Meta
    complies with Meta's Platform Terms and Developer Policies.
  </p>

  <h2>The iOS app</h2>
  <p>
    The TradeCommand app for iPhone and iPad shows the same service as app.tradecommand.com.au. It
    asks for three permissions, and each one is optional:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Notifications,</strong> to tell you about new jobs, messages and tasks.</li>
    <li><strong>Camera,</strong> only when you take a photo to attach to a job.</li>
    <li><strong>Location,</strong> only at the moment you clock in or out.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app does not track you across other apps or websites, and it contains no advertising. You
    can delete your account in the app from your profile.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep business records for as long as the business keeps its account, because the business
    needs them to run. When a business closes its account, we delete its data within 30 days, apart
    from records we must keep by law and from backups, which expire on their own cycle. See our
    <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a> for how to request deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit. Access tokens for connected services are encrypted at rest.
    Access to production systems is limited to the people who operate the service. No system is
    perfectly secure, and we will tell affected people and the regulator about a data breach where
    the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct
    it. If you are a client or contact of a business that uses the service, you can also ask that
    business directly, since it controls the record. We respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:privacy@tradecommand.com.au">privacy@tradecommand.com.au</a>, or write to
    TC Systems Pty Ltd, 6 Lyster Street, Coffs Harbour NSW 2450, Australia. If you are not satisfied
    with our response, you can complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
    <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au">oaic.gov.au</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We update this policy when the service changes. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
</Legal>
